# ⭐ The most important lesson from your exercise

You made a very good transition from:

> **"What YAML lines do I copy?"**

to:

> **"What needs to happen to deploy my FastAPI application?"**

That's exactly the transition you need.

But now take it one level further.

Whenever you design a pipeline, ask these **8 questions**:

| Question                            | Your Caregence answer     |
| ----------------------------------- | ------------------------- |
| 1. What triggers it?                | Manual / push             |
| 2. What code?                       | GitHub repository         |
| 3. What runtime?                    | Python                    |
| 4. What dependencies?               | requirements.txt          |
| 5. How do I validate?               | Tests / lint / validation |
| 6. Where do I deploy?               | EC2                       |
| 7. How do I run it?                 | Supervisor                |
| 8. How do I know deployment worked? | Status + health check     |

Then add the **production questions**:

```text
What if deployment fails?
       ↓
Rollback?

What if server already has running application?
       ↓
Backup?

What secrets are required?
       ↓
GitHub Secrets / Environment Secrets?

Who can deploy Production?
       ↓
Environment approval?

How do I authenticate to AWS/EC2?
       ↓
OIDC / SSM / SSH?

How do I know exactly what version was deployed?
       ↓
Commit SHA / release / artifact?
```

**If you can answer those questions, you can design a CI/CD pipeline.** The exact YAML syntax can always be looked up in the current official documentation. That's normal—even experienced DevOps engineers look up action versions and syntax.
